  "description": "This application is for a proposed outbuilding to the rear of the residential property for use incidental to the enjoyment of the dwelllinghouse.\nIt is maintained that the constructed outbuilding meets all the necessary planning tests and objectives set by adopted planning policy, based upon the following principal reasons:\n1) Use – the use as a residential garden room remains incidental to the enjoyment of the dwellinghouse and does not result in a change of use from C3 residential. To provide further comfort on this point, the constructed outbuilding does not contain the facilities necessary for providing separate, self-contained residential accommodation, nor would it be capable of severance from the main house with separate access.\n2) Siting and Character – the residential outbuilding is located in the rear garden amenity area. Furthermore, the outbuilding is not readily visible from within the street scene and therefore is not a visible or dominant feature from within the public highway and public domain.\n3) Design and external appearance – The building will be constructed to a maximum overall hight of 2.5m. The new building is of very high quality and finish incorporating the latest design and building standards, composite cladding and UPVC doors and windows.\n4) Scale – The outbuilding remains single storey in height at 2.5m reflecting the character of neighbouring outbuildings occupying similar plots within the rearmost portion of their respective residential gardens.\n5) Overdevelopment - The single storey outbuilding occupies a minor portion of the overall rear garden curtilage area. It therefore does not constitute overdevelopment of the host plot with the majority of the rear garden amenity area remaining free of built development footprint and the scale of the outbuilding remaining subordinate to that of the main house.",
